※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4633

※ A place reached through a reference parameter is the caller's, and what is
※ written there is read after the call has ended, so it has to last that long:
※ made in `⎕heap` or in the image.  A string made anywhere else is copied into
※ `⎕heap` on the way in, as an answer is; a record holding one cannot be copied
※ yet, and one made in an arena given back on the way out is refused.

type Inner = s: str
type Box = inner: Inner

@[impure]
fn keep(b: &mut Box):
    let pool: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(pool)
    b⌖.inner ← Inner(.s ← "a" ⧺ "b" in pool)

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
